# Standard Rust build output. The repo-root `.gitignore` only ignores a
# top-level `/target` (the root Cargo workspace's), which this crate's
# `[workspace]` isolation (see Cargo.toml) deliberately does not share --
# so it needs its own ignore rule here.
/target

# Tauri's codegen output. `tauri-build` writes `gen/schemas/*.json` (the ACL
# capability and permission manifests) on every build, so this directory
# appeared the first time this crate was compiled on macOS -- untracked and,
# until this rule, not ignored either.
#
# Narrowed to `/gen/schemas` rather than all of `/gen` on purpose: Tauri's
# mobile targets put `gen/android` and `gen/apple` under the same directory and
# those ARE meant to be committed. Ignoring the whole `/gen` would silently
# swallow them if this project ever adds a mobile target.
#
# This is only the first line of defence. CI-10 (scripts/ci.sh) is the last one
# and does NOT cover this path -- its name whitelist is node_modules / target /
# dist / .pnpm, so a forced `git add` of this directory still passes CI
# (measured, see docs/STATUS.md P2 #14).
/gen/schemas
